## 1. Definitions

For the purposes of this License:

**“Software”** means the LX-VOXEL source code, object code, libraries, tools, documentation, configuration files, reference implementations, and other materials distributed under this License.

**“Licensor”** means Kelvin Eller, or any successor explicitly designated as the copyright holder or authorized licensor of LX-VOXEL.

**“You”** means any individual or legal entity exercising rights granted under this License.

**“Modified Version”** means any modification, adaptation, port, translation, fork, derivative work, or other version based substantially on the Software.

**“Integrated Product”** means a product, application, game, operating system, hardware device, media system, service, or other larger work in which the Software is used only as a component and where the primary commercial value of that product does not consist of providing LX-VOXEL itself.

**“Standalone Codec Product”** means any codec, codec library, SDK, software package, API, service, command-line tool, transcoding product, or substantially equivalent offering whose primary purpose or commercial value consists of providing the functionality of the Software or a Modified Version.

**“Streaming Service”** means an online service that transmits or makes available audio content to end users through live streaming, on-demand streaming, personalized streaming, internet radio, cloud-based playback, or substantially equivalent network delivery.

**“LX-VOXEL Streaming User”** means a unique end user who, during a calendar month, is actually delivered, offered, or served audio encoded using LX-VOXEL through a Streaming Service.

Users who do not receive LX-VOXEL encoded audio are not LX-VOXEL Streaming Users for the purposes of this License.

**“Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users”** means the number of unique LX-VOXEL Streaming Users during a calendar month.

