## 5. Streaming Services

### 5.1 Free Streaming Use

A Streaming Service may use LX-VOXEL without payment of a streaming license fee where the Streaming Service has fewer than:

**1,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users.**

This permission applies to commercial and non-commercial Streaming Services.

No streaming license fee is required merely because:

a. a service supports LX-VOXEL decoding;

b. a service supports uploading or downloading LX-VOXEL files;

c. LX-VOXEL is used internally for testing, development, archival, evaluation, research, or quality comparison;

d. a service has more than 1,000,000 total users but fewer than 1,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users; or

e. LX-VOXEL support exists in software distributed to users but LX-VOXEL encoded audio is not delivered by the Streaming Service itself.

### 5.2 Medium Streaming License

Where a Streaming Service has:

**1,000,000 or more, but fewer than 15,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users,**

the operator must obtain an **LX-VOXEL Medium Streaming License**.

The published price for LX-VOXEL Source License 1.2 is:

**€10,000 EUR per year.**

The Medium Streaming License is intended to provide a low-friction commercial path for substantial deployments that have not yet reached Large Streaming scale.

### 5.3 Large Streaming License

A Streaming Service becomes subject to the **LX-VOXEL Large Streaming License** once it reaches or exceeds:

**15,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users**

during any calendar month.

The published price for LX-VOXEL Source License 1.2 is:

**€10,000 EUR per month.**

Once the Large Streaming threshold has been reached, the Streaming Service shall remain classified as a Large Streaming Service for a minimum period of **twelve (12) consecutive months**, regardless of ordinary fluctuations in Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users during that period.

After the initial twelve-month Large Streaming period, the Streaming Service may qualify for reclassification to the Medium Streaming License only where its average Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users during the preceding three complete calendar months is below 15,000,000.

Temporary, seasonal, technical, geographic, promotional, rollout-related, or ordinary fluctuations below the Large Streaming threshold do not automatically terminate or reduce the Large Streaming License obligation.

A Streaming Service that is reclassified below the Large Streaming tier and subsequently again reaches or exceeds 15,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users begins a new twelve-month Large Streaming License period.

### 5.4 Measurement and Qualification

For Free and Medium Streaming Use, the applicable tier is determined using Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users as defined in Section 1.

A Streaming Service may conduct a reasonable technical trial, beta test, or staged deployment without immediately becoming subject to a paid Streaming License, provided that the deployment remains below 1,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users.

Once a Streaming Service reaches or exceeds 1,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users, the operator must obtain the applicable Streaming License within 60 days.

For avoidance of doubt, the Large Streaming classification rules in Section 5.3 control once the 15,000,000-user threshold has been reached.

### 5.5 No Usage-Based Royalty

Except for the fixed Medium and Large Streaming License fees described above, there is:

a. no per-stream royalty;

b. no per-minute royalty;

c. no per-song royalty;

d. no per-byte royalty;

e. no revenue share; and

f. no additional charge based solely on the quantity of LX-VOXEL encoded content transmitted.

The Large Streaming License is billed as a fixed monthly license during the applicable Large Streaming classification period.

### 5.6 Scope of Streaming License

Payment of the applicable Streaming License permits the licensed Streaming Service to use LX-VOXEL for its covered streaming operations during the applicable license period, subject to the remaining terms of this License.

Unless separately agreed, the Streaming License does not grant:

a. ownership of LX-VOXEL;

b. exclusive rights;

c. trademark ownership;

d. the right to commercially resell LX-VOXEL as a Standalone Codec Product; or

e. rights outside those otherwise granted by this License.

### 5.7 Enterprise Agreements for Streaming Services

A Streaming Service may request an LX-VOXEL Enterprise License or Enterprise Agreement under Section 18A for custom implementation, integration, support, service-level commitments, custom commercial terms, or other enterprise requirements.

An Enterprise Agreement may replace the standard pricing or terms of this Section only where the Licensor and the applicable Streaming Service expressly agree to that replacement in writing.

