## 15. Compliance and Records for Paid Streaming Use

A Streaming Service subject to Section 5 must maintain records reasonably sufficient to determine its applicable LX-VOXEL Streaming License tier and, where applicable, the beginning and duration of a Large Streaming classification period.

The Licensor may request written confirmation of the approximate number of Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users and the information reasonably necessary to verify the applicable tier no more than once per calendar year unless there is a reasonable basis to believe that a material licensing violation has occurred.

Nothing in this Section requires disclosure of personally identifiable end-user information.

Aggregate usage figures are sufficient.

