## 23. Summary of Intended Use

This Section is explanatory only. If it conflicts with another provision of this License, the substantive provisions above control.

The intended licensing model is:

**Free:**
- personal use;
- education;
- academic research;
- commercial applications;
- media players;
- games;
- operating systems;
- audio workstations;
- broadcasting applications;
- OBS-style applications;
- hardware devices;
- local encoding and decoding;
- commercial applications containing LX-VOXEL;
- open-source and source-available projects;
- internal testing;
- codec evaluation;
- Streaming Services with fewer than 1,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users.

**€10,000/year Medium Streaming License:**
- 1,000,000 to fewer than 15,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users.

**€10,000/month Large Streaming License:**
- triggered when a Streaming Service reaches 15,000,000 or more Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users;
- remains in effect for a minimum of 12 consecutive months after qualification;
- may be reclassified after that period only where the preceding three-month average is below 15,000,000 Monthly LX-VOXEL Streaming Users.

**Enterprise License — pricing on request:**
- available to Streaming Services and non-streaming organizations;
- intended for custom implementations, platform ports, hardware/DSP optimization, integration assistance, priority support, SLAs, private builds, custom rights, consulting, research, certification, or other enterprise requirements;
- optional unless a use requires rights not otherwise granted by this License;
- may replace standard Streaming License terms only by express written agreement.

There are no standard per-stream, per-song, per-minute, per-byte, or revenue-share royalties.

The purpose of the Streaming License is to allow broad and low-friction adoption of LX-VOXEL while requiring large-scale commercial streaming deployments to financially support the continued development, maintenance, and ecosystem of LX-VOXEL.

The purpose of the Enterprise License is to allow organizations with specialized technical or commercial requirements to directly fund custom engineering, integration, support, maintenance, and professional development of the LX-VOXEL ecosystem.

